      "role": "EN-READ-F",
      "source": "reading.text",
      "tts_text": "Built from stone taken from the nearby quarry, the footbridge has served the village for generations. After a severe flood, a survey completed by local engineers found that one abutment needed attention. The archway, inspected from both banks, remained firm, but a railing loosened during the storm. Workers mixed fresh mortar and replaced several blocks. The heritage group recorded each change before reopening the path. A notice placed beside the mill explains which parts were restored. Visitors can now cross safely, although the team will inspect the bridge again after the winter rains.",
